Daniel.Brunelle@nrc.ca (Daniel Brunelle) wrote:
>I connected a standard DAT tape drive (form Archive corporation model 
>4354XP) on a Alpha Box running OSF/1.
>  
>How do I create the device driver for it ?
>
>I tried :
>
># cd /dev
># ./MAKEDEV rmt
>MAKEDEV: special files(s) for rmt:
>MAKEDEV: unknown device in: rmt

Configure your kernel to detect the tape (/usr/sys/conf/HOSTNAME)
add a line like:
device tape     tz#        at asc0      drive     #*8
(#=scsi ID of your streamer)


build the new kernel

reboot

# cd /dev
/MAKEDEV/tz#         (#=scsi ID of your streamer)

and devices like rmt0h, rmt0l, etc. are build.

Joerg
