In article <3sovm8$iph@news-rocq.inria.fr>,  <piumarta@epaf.inria.fr> wrote:
>I'm investigating the possibility of modifying a garbage collector to
>work with DEC's pthreads under OSF/1.  For this I need to be able to
>determine the stack limits for each thread, but I can't find any
>information on how to do this.
>

To get the stack size of a thread call the pthread_attr_getstacksize 
routine. I have used this routine on VMS and it works fine. Never tried 
it on OSF/1 (although the pthread interface is supposed to be compatible).
This routine will give you the stack size of the thread when it was created,
however, it does not tell you the current size of the stack.



