In article <3s7b0p$2a7@news.xmission.com>, fci  <fci@xmission.com> wrote:
>I am trying to get ahold of some user documentation pertaining to 
>the Digital 4mm DAT autoloder.  We are currently using this under 
>ULTRIX on a DECStation 5000, but we don't know how to utilize the 
>multi-tape capability.

We use the autoloader on Digital UNIX. I simply do a "mt offline".
This ejects the tape and loads the next one. If it was the last tape,
no tape is loaded.

I don't know what happens if you reach the end of the first tape.
Please post when you find out.

There are some switches documented in the "TLZ06 Cassette Tape Drive"
"Owner's Manual" (EK-TLZ06-OM.004 July 1993) Chapter 7 "TLZ6L Auto Loader".
But I think you should not change these settings.
(SW1-1+2 display language, SW1-3 continuous cycle, SW1-4 display intensity, 
SW2-1 display orientation, SW2-2 auto-load, the other SWs are Reserved)
To access the switches the drawer must be in outside position.
They are on top of the drive. I think you also have to remove
the drive from it's box. Do not change the SCSI ID switches S1-S8!

The continuous cycle mode is dangerous, as it may overwrite 
the first tape after it reaches the end of the last tape.

Sequential and random cassette access is available via SCSI commands.

Does anybody use Polycenter Networker Save and Restore
in combination with the autoloader?

>Thanks,
>Scott Heffield
