The following short c program produces two different result by
using -O3 and -O (or no optimization at all):

#include <stdio.h>
#include <math.h>

main() {
     double sig( double x, double gain, double thresh);
     double x;
     for (x=(-4.0); x<4.1; x+=1.0) {
          printf("%f %f\n", x, sig(x,1.0,0.0) );
     }
}

double sig( double x, double gain, double thresh) {
     return( 1.0 / ( 1.0 + exp( - (gain) * ( x - thresh ) ) ) );
}


Using -O or no opti: (correct result, same result on SUN, HP, Ultrix, etc)

-4.000000 0.017986
-3.000000 0.047426
-2.000000 0.119203
-1.000000 0.268941
0.000000 0.500000
1.000000 0.731059
2.000000 0.880797
3.000000 0.952574
4.000000 0.982014

Using -O3:	(WRONG!)

-4.000000 0.982014
-3.000000 0.952574
-2.000000 0.880797
-1.000000 0.731059
0.000000 0.500000
1.000000 0.268941
2.000000 0.119203
3.000000 0.047426
4.000000 0.017986

Any hints or help would be appreciated!

