I'm no expert on OSF/1, or networking, so please view this response with
caution.  However, the messages sound like it's an ethernet problem.  We've had
problems in the past on our OpenVMS cluster, with network errors.  Very often
these were found to be due to the physical bits of cable between bits of
hardware exceeding the length limits defined by the ethernet standards.  Each
device also has an equivalent length to allow for propagation of the packets
through it.  I advise you to check all the lengths of cables and equipment on
your network against the ethernet standard.  If they're too long, you'll find
your network can slow down to a snail's pace due to all the retransmits that
are required for the machines to understand each other.

