In article <3sudi9$mq6@news.informix.com> pcaffrey@PROBLEM_WITH_INEWS_GATEWAY_FILE (Paul Caffrey) writes:
>Hi,
>
>Is there a summary of the differences between OSF/1 and SVR4? Any FAQs,
>commercial publications etc?
>

Digital has an internally published compatibility guide. The document in
question was developed using external consultants, and is extremely
comprehensive. In fact, one thing I'd warn against is that the document may
lead you to believe that the differences are larger than they actually are.
That's because the level of detail is almost annoying, down to trivial 
differences in the contents of header files.

You can get it on the Web in PostScript form at

http://www.digital.com/info/key-dec-osf1-index.html

Look for the "System V Compatibility User's Guide DEC OSF/1 Version 1.2".

You might also want to get the most up-to-date docs on the
"System V Environment for DEC OSF/1[R] V3.2".

Basically, the compatibility with SVR4 is extraordinarily good - far better
than HP/UX or even Solaris, even without the optional environment. The added
optional environment will give you stuff like SVR4 style system administration
commands.

Hope that helps.

Eric Osborne
