In article <3r4ppg$k7s@decsys.vsb.cz> Jakub Nantl <root@albert.opf.slu.cz>
writes:
> We have just installed Enhanced Security, from this time we are not able to
> connect to our DEC using Xappeal (Dos emul of xterm). Exactly the conection is
> made but server complains "Cannot find database info on this terminal"

You need to add a line to the file /etc/auth/system/ttys, something like

albert\:0:t_devname=albert\:0:t_xdisplay:t_login_timeout#0:chkent:

and a line to the file /etc/auth/system/devassign, something like

albert\:0:v_devs=albert\:0,albert.opf.slu.cz\:0,193.84.208.62\:0:v_type=xdisplay:chkent:

You may also want to play with /etc/securettys (though this is not
C2-specific).

Hope this helps.

