	Hi

	If you get to console prompt ">>>" and run command show dev
	you should see something like
	DKA400 a/4/0 rodisk rm rrd43 and so on
	The DK refer to a SCSI disk device and rrd43 is your cdrom .
	You also could use the following procedure to find out you cdrom :

	# file /dev/rrz*c
	This command output give some /dev/rrz?c .. .. RRD?? 
	This is your cdrom dev.

	# mkdir /cdrom
	This create a mount point for cdrom
	
	#mount -r /dev/rz?c /cdrom
	This is usually /dev/rz4c but check it before using 4.
	This will mount your cdrom for you.
	# cd /cdrom
	you are ready to see what you have on cd,assuming cd file-system 
	is unix filesystem. I hope this work.
	 
	
