In article <hickman.95Jun23141611@frodo> hickman@frodo writes:
hickman> Whenever I get close to 7MB for the object library
hickman> file, ar croaks saying that the file system is full
[...]
hickman> There does not appear to be any doc describing ways to change
hickman> this upper limit.

By default ar uses /tmp to build the intermediate archive, so the size
of the archive is limited to the size of the free space in /tmp.  The
'l' flag tells ar to use the local directory for intermediates, or you
can set the the TMPDIR environment variable to someplace with more
space.  This is all documented in the ar man page.

p.s.  Steve, please configure your news system to include a valid
return address in the headers?  'hickman@frodo' doesn't do it for most
of us.

