In article <3r9sct$b2v@ns.neptune.com>,
Tom Techoueyres <tom@neptune.com> wrote:
>Hello
>
>We are running sendmail on an alpha 2100 running osf/1, but when we try to 
>retrieve mail from the server using eudora on a pc workstation, we get a 
>"connection refused". Are there parameters in the sendmail.cf  file that we 
>should configure for a pc workstation to be able to retrieve mail from the 
>mail server?
>I would appreciate any help!

Eudora requires a POP (post office protocol) server.  Sendmail is NOT a
POP server.  Digital do supply a POP server as part of the MH subset,
or you can pick up the BSD POP server from most FTP sites.  Note that the
BSD server needs to be modifed if you are running Enhanced Security.

