In article <3scmi3$pck@ixnews6.ix.netcom.com>
t-l-c@ix.netcom.com (Charlie Giampaolo ) wrote:

> Why is it that I have to type ./ then the executable file name.  Is
> there somthing to change in my profile??

Because the current directory isn't in your path. This stops
scenarios such as the following:

1) user creates script called ls which deletes /etc/passwd
2) user calls you and says "hey, there's a funny file in my directory"
3) you (logged in as root) cd to the user's directory and type ls
4) havoc

This omission of "." in the path is deliberate, not accidental. Change
it at your own risk.

PJDM
