It is possible to load file system drivers into DEC OSF/1 v3.X kernels
(v2.x and v1.x don't have loadable kernel module support).  Our product
(ClearCase) does exactly that, and has done so since September 1994
(when we added V3.0 support).  I sent some mail to Transarc to encourage
them to make their AFS modules loadable; maybe they'll do that in a
future release.

The device driver documentation DEC provides is almost sufficient for
file systems.  They suggest that you can't load filesystems, but you
really can as long as you know how to get into and out of the file
system switch table (and there are system routines that do this).

I particularly like their parameter (re-)configuration stuff--it's easy
to reconfigure parameters on the fly, and you only have to unload/reload
to get "static" parameters to change.  You don't have to reboot to get
them to stick (like you do with /etc/system on solaris).
