summary: DEC 3000/300X performance is horrible under multiuser loads with 3.2.

	I'm writing the group because of a lack of response from
Digital Support, Digital Engineering, and the Alpha Port Group.

	We are a small software developer engaged in porting a fairly
large database engine from ULTRIX to OSF/1. We have four Alphas for
development, while most of our engineers use MIPS workstations. The
Alphas are DEC 3000/300Xs, two with 128MB of memory and two with
64MB. The problems we see occure worst during compile/linking. If a
compile or link is initiated, multiprocessing ceases. The disk goes
crazy and the display essentially freezes.....an xclock with a second
hand stops and mouse actions can take minutes to be responded to.
DEC's advice has been to tinker with the UBC parameters, which has
been of no use.
	This is the second time we've been in this fix. Under OSF/1
3.0 we had similar problems. Tinkering with UBC parameters did not
improve behavior, but DEC Support did provide patches that calmed the
crazy paging of the disk and allowed the Alpha to achieve the balanced
response seen on the MIPS. Now, we have had to move onto 3.2 to run
some third party software. Our performance has once again gone to
hell. DEC Support claims there is nothing to fix....no patches in the
cupboard to improve the multiprocessing disaster.

	Has anyone solved this problem??? Are there patches to 3.2 to
make its multiprocessing behavior decent?? Please let us know!!

							--Sid

