Note that the above will only show the CDROM if that SCSI ID has
been built into the kernel (or if you've booted genvmunix).

If you know what the SCSI ID is of your CD, then add 8 to it
and:

cd /dev
/MAKEDEV rz# , where # is the id of your CD plus 8
file /dev/rrz#c, where # is the id of your CD plus 8

This should give you a line indicating that it found the CDROM
device.

Good luck,
Dave



