including Ultrix, is very compatible with SUN OS and BSDism. 

I have to maintain the workstation in my office, plus several
other DEC 3000/300 in our department.  So I am an amature
adiministrator.  The more than ten year UNIX experiences
usually get me over minor to moderate software/administrative
problems.

However, recently I got more frustrated with DEC OSF/Digital
UNIX.  For a number of problems, such as SLIP, PPP, serial port,
anonymous FTP,  I could not find solutions from the book reader.
Asking help to DEC through this news group usually  got zero
answers. For instance, my anonymous FTP works, but it cannot
support "tar.gz" retrieval.  I cannot find any possible help.
