I'm running AdvFS as my news spool. I started it in 3.0 before I found out
about the metadata problem, though... It bit us right before we moved from
a 3000 to our current 2100, and so I took that opportunity to format up a
new disk on 3.2A, and used the -x option to specify a huge metadata extent.
(The 3.2 installtion guide discusses the problem, and suggests a value for
-x based on number of files; I doubled their recommendation.)

On the plus side, AdvFS *greatly* improves news performance, as measured by
articles received per second. On the minus side, I'm hopping from one leg to
the other waiting for the hammer to fall...

