In article <1995Jun15.161049.1480@queens-belfast.ac.uk>, ed says...
>When he attempts to run the task he obtains a report indicating 
insufficient
>swap space (currently avail: Physical Memory 64MB, Total swap space 
428MB),
>upon contacting MATHWORKS Inc.  he was told to have the system manager 
increase
>the swap space available. 

Check process limit on datasize (% limit). There are two configuration 
parameters in the kernel configuration file - dfldsiz and maxdsiz which 
govern the default datasize and maximum datasize for processes. I added a 
line to Matlab users .login to increase the datasize limit to the 
maximum. That solved a similar problem here (although they were massaging 
massive datasets).

Don




