In article <Rg3d+8F.donald44@delphi.com>, Donald Gray <donald44@delphi.com> writes:
|>
|>I'am tring to use RSH from a HP to an ALPHA. I have set up hosts.equiv
|>and .rhosts. Root logins are enabled from anywhere. but I still get
|>a permission denied error. It works fine from ALPHA to HP and I can
|>login to the ALPHA usind root. However rlogin is requiring a password.
|>Any help would be greatly appricated.
|>						Thanks,
|>						D-Man
|>


According to the rsh man page, when using the root ID for rsh, the hosts.equiv
file does not come into play.  Instead, you need to have an appropriate /.rhosts
file.

So there is likely something wrong with you /.rhosts file.

1) If you are superuser when you run rsh, an entry in /.rhosts with just your
hostname will work.

2) If you aren't superuser when you run rsh, an entry in /.rhosts with your
hostname and username will work.

3) If #1 or #2 aren't the problem, then it is very likely that the problem is
due to /.rhosts not being owned by root and/or not having a mode of 600.

Dave




