: look at the processes, there is a job called "pvRm" running, and it gets

pvRm is the process talking to the high-performance card. I always restart
the server after logging off (which seems to be happening to you already)
by either adding the correct resource to the xdm resource file or by adding
the -terminate option to the Xserver.conf file. Restarting the server
allows memory that may have been used by the old server process to be
released back to the system - using PEX in structure store mode may cause
the server to grow pretty large. That growth is a result of the semantics
of malloc & free (actually, the C library malloc call never sbrks to a 
previous address).

Maybe someday we'll get a server with mmap() instead of malloc in the PEX
structure code so we won't have this problem - when the user connection
to the display terminates it could release the associated memory.
