In article <3rst5b$i3c@news1.WING.NET>, Mark Saltzman (marks@wing.net) wrote:
> I'm considering using a DEC Alpha for a large WWW server project.  I've heard

> Any opinions on this?  How secure/insecure is it out of the box?  
> How reliable?

In our experience, reliability and support have been horrendous.

We've had such serious reliability problems on our main Internet server
machine (an Alpha 3000/800 running OSF/1 3.0) that our next server will 
not be an Alpha/OSF machine.

We've had hardware problems (we're on the machine's replacement's replacement),
software problems (2-3 times a day panics due to file system problems),
feature set problems (a long, long list), and support problems (it took
repeated calls up the chain to Vice Presidents to be be taken seriously,
and then, in the middle, the support people vanished, on to other crises).

There are, of course, people who swear that this stuff is rock solid, so
your mileage may vary.

