Umm, perhaps you should rethink the phrasing of "non-standard".  SCO Unix
*IS* based on MANY standards, as are all the Unixes.  And the days of
ODT 1.1, and even 2.0 are LONG since over (see data on OS 5.0).

Having used ODT 1.0/1.1, I can confirm that the development system was
SERIOUSLY broken.  And it was still broken in 2.0.  But most all my
problems disappeared with 3.0's development system.  And 5.0's development
system is code taken from SVR4.

The remaining Unixes in the current market are closer than ever before
(I wish they were even closer still, however).

