I think that it's a pretty good Unix that has a SYSVR4 feel with Berk
tools available as well.  IMHO it's better in this respect than Solaris.   I
have built just about everything under the sun (no pun intended) on it in
the last 3 years with few problems (some problems with 64bit issues on
broken code but you're going to encounter that on a lot of Unices in the
near future).  The folks I'm currently contracting for (a major wantabe
Internet Service Provider) just bought 100 Alphas for their WWW server farm
(well I said major :-) .  Performance is great, support is less than great
but getting better.  The OS is brick solid as far as I can see at 3.x and
feels like a SYSVR4 from a coding and operations standpoint.  Many parts
of DEC still don't understand Unix (sell ya VMS sonny ? No, you want the
snakeoil !!!? :-)  but there are some very bright folks in UEG if you can
get to them.  

Summary: Portation is a snap, it * is * SVR4 in that respect and it goes
like hell :-) but don't expect to get a lot of questions answered without
a fight :-)

OB Disclaimer:  I worked for DECAthena for a couple of years but we had 7
Unices and we loved them all equally ( and no, we didn't do no stinking
VMS )

Jeff Tyler
PSA




