Robert Cerniglia <peitechs@fast.net> writes:
>I'm trying to find somebody who can tell me where to find or how to
>write a script that will display my Current working directory as my system
>prompt.

It depends on which shell you use.  Certain shells allow format
characters in the prompt string which expand to the current path.  I
know bash does and I believe tcsh does also; others may as well, but I
don't use them.  The man page for your shell should describe special
prompt codes.

I don't know if csh allows prompt codes.  If note and you're using
csh, you can do something like
  alias cd 'cd \!*; set prompt=$cwd%'
I'm not a csh user and there may be easier ways.  Again, see the man
page.
