Donald Gray <donald44@delphi.com> writes:

>I'am tring to use RSH from a HP to an ALPHA. I have set up hosts.equiv
>and .rhosts. Root logins are enabled from anywhere. but I still get
>a permission denied error. It works fine from ALPHA to HP and I can
>login to the ALPHA usind root. However rlogin is requiring a password.
>Any help would be greatly appricated.

OSF1 ships with only /dev/console, local:0, :0 in the /etc/securettys
file.  You would have to add "ptys" to /etc/securettys as well as a
/.rhosts or a hosts.equiv entry to allow a remote root shell.

#  /etc/securettys
# 
#  Note: Each entry in this file represents a device (secure device) 
#  from which root login is permitted.  For, pseudo ttys (ptys) a 
#  single keyword entry "ptys" means all ptys are to be treated as being
#  secure.  Note that the entry is "ptys" and not prefixed by /dev
#  as is customary for the other physical devices.  The absence of
#  this key word implies that root login will not be permitted from 
#  all ptys.  X displays are indicated with the display name.



Paul
