The DEC Fortran Language Reference Manual says (Page 10-31):

Scratch files (STATUS='SCRATCH') are created in the user's working directory
and are visible while they are open.

I suspect this is not true. On an Alpha system running OSF/1 3.2 scratch files
are always created in /tmp and not in the user's working directory; they are
called something like /tmp/aaaaa3efa.

Is there a simple way to specify a default path for scratch files, preferably
through an environment variable? The manual seems to be silent on this point.
I know about the FILE and DEFAULTFILE keywords in the OPEN statement, and about
the FORTx environment variable, but that's not quite what I want. On an AIX
system with xlf, the environment variable TMPDIR does what I need.
