> significant? Is it worth using AdvFS if the only thing we really want
> is striping (over two disks in this case)? (BTW: we can't stripe
> without AdvFS, can we?)

You can't use AdvFS to stripe file systems. It only stripes files. If you
want to stripe volumes, use LSM. I have one customer who uses LSM to
stripe 6 RZ26Ls and mirror them with another 6, with AdvFS on top.
Performance is satisfactory. 8-)

Last week, one of the disks went bad, and they didn't notice for three
days until I visited and pointed it out. By the end of the day, the disk
was replaced and the mirror was rebuilt without rebooting the system
or disturbing the users.

I would use both: LSM for performance, and AdvFS for convenience.

PJDM
