Actually that's where I started this sad and rather painful journey.
I've implemented the algorithm exactly as it is described.  My code
generates CRCs which are the same as those generated by NetBSD's
cksum(1).  (I grabbed the [publicly available] NetBSD cksum(1) source
from an FTP site somewhere.)  The OSF/1 cksum(1) in /bin steadfastly
generates something different.

I've resorted to trying variations on the theme in an attempt to devine
the algorithm used.  I've tried not inverting the result; I've tried
starting with all CRC bits set; and I've tried reversing the bytes
before computing and reversing the result (pkzip uses this approach).
No dice.

I guess I'm just experiencing the beauty of standards: there are just so
darn many to choose from.  Sigh.

