S> COFF format alpha shared library, demand paged executable or object
S> module not stripped - version 3.11-4

S> but none of the options I have seen for ld seem to create one of these.

All you need to do is build build your modules, then link them
together into a shared library using the proper flags.  This isn't
explained too well in the ld man page, but once you know what to do,
it's pretty simple.  For example:

	ar rcu tmp.a foo.o bar.o 
	ld -o libtmp.so -shared -expect_unresolved "*" -s -all tmp.a

The -expect_unresolved "*" isn't really needed, but it does serve to
keep ld quieter.  Hope this helps.

John

