X-Deja-AN: 104317360
distribution: world
references: <3q221n$o6b@fermat.mayo.edu> <3q4juh$5ea@lead.zk3.dec.com> <JOHN.95Jun7160403@avante.WPI.EDU>
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: lueck@zk3.dec.com (Greg Lueck Development Environment)
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


John,

It appears that your application free's NULL pointers a lot.  By default,
Third Degree reports these in the output file.  Third also has a limit of
500 diagnostics, after which it just dies.  This is the limit you seem
to be hitting.

You can tell Third to ignore free's of NULL pointers by creating a .3rd file
with the line

ignore	fon

You can read /usr/lib/atom/doc/3rd.ps for more information about the .3rd
file.


