keywords: include prototypes osf1v3
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1
summary: Wrong prototype declarations in include files

Having included 'sys/ioctl.h' when compiling with 'gcc -Wall' I still
got that annoying warning: implicit declaration of function `ioctl'.

Looking in sys/ioctl.h reveals the following:

#ifndef _KERNEL
#ifdef _NO_PROTO
extern int      ioctl();
#else
#if defined(__STDC__) || defined(__cplusplus)
#if defined(__cplusplus)
extern "C"
{
extern int      ioctl(int, int, ...);
}
#endif
#endif
#endif /* _NO_PROTO */
#endif /* _KERNEL */

So we will *never* get a prototype declaration with an ansi-c compiler :-(

If someone at digital is listening, how about changing this stuff to:

...
#if defined(__STDC__) || defined(__cplusplus)
#if defined(__cplusplus)
extern "C"
{
#endif
extern int      ioctl(int, int, ...);
#if defined(__cplusplus)
}
#endif
#endif
...


No, I don't know how many of the 815 include files of osf/1 also have
this error and I *won't* check :-{

Klaus

