In article <stouffer-0606951031030001@168.143.9.106>, stouffer@clark.net (Edward Stouffer) writes:
> We have a DEC 7000 running OSF/1 version 2.0A. On it we have Pathworks
> 5.0D with TCP/IP. As well, we have Oracle 7.0.14 with CA-ManMan/X.
> 
> When we run Pathworks w/o Oracle it is fine. When we run Oracle w/o
> Pathworks all is well. When we run them both, the run queue depth rapidly
> gets to 4 and Pathworks being having 10-40 second pauses in performance.
> This is with 5 Oracle users and 5 Pathworks connections and nothing else.

FIY, we're running Oracle 7.0.16 (runtime) with 2-5 users, PW5.0D with about
50 users and aditionally a NFS/NIS server service with 12 users. All this
on a simple 3000-600s with 192MB RAM without any performance problems under
OSF/1 2.0 rev.250.

But I remember having had one problem after the Oracle installation: Have
a look at your var/adm/syslog.dated/.../kern.log files. If they're crammed
with 'vmunix: vnode table full' messages (in such a case, the system is even
too busy for sending this to the console!), you have to increase the maxusers
parameter in the kernel config file, I'd suggest 128 or even 256.

hope this helps,
Eric



