1. If you read through the doc set it will make reference to matrix.conf,
which it says you can't change. To su to root, you must be in the system
group in /etc/group.

3. Yes, you probably do need kernel support. The auto-config'd kernel
created from the FIS probably didn't see the monitor and built no support.
Probably the easiest way is to look the the GENERIC (or BINARY in some
revs) kernel config file in /sys/conf for the possible entries and it is
hopefully documented. You may need a MAKEDEV also after that. As well, you
may need a tty entry for :0.

