writes:
|> 
|> I've just put a Micropolis 9Gb disk on an Alpha 200 4/233 with no problem
|> yet! Does the rotational speed actually affect anything, such as 
|> performance?
 
As my understanding goes (which admittedly isn't perfect), the rotational
speed given by disklabel is always 3600 rpm, regardless of what the disk
drive is doing - it is just there for information.  Whatever value it is
given will not actually affect the disk - if you changed it to 200000 rpm,
I don't think it would change the speed of the disk.  If you want to
set it to the actual disk speed, for your information only, then perhaps
you could try changing it with disklabel -e ....?

