We have a 3000 model 800, 256 MB RAM, 6 GB disk, with 9,000 active users
and 30,000 user accounts.  It slows down when there are more than 150
simultaneous users, probably from lack of RAM. 

We are providing internet access and E-mail through a gopher-look-alike
Menu Shell written here.  The user community is "all students - full and
part time, undergrad, graduate, and medical, main and regional campuses."

We will be upgrading later this summer to a 2100 5/250 with 512 MB RAM
and at least 10 GB disk. 

Contention on access to the password file appears to be a major source of
the RAM shortage:  finger and password re-setting.  We have recently
improved this by writing a more efficient version of the utility we have
to permit staff to reset passwords to the student's default.

