>to move the o.s. to C2 security level, or there are other solutions  ? 

Kerberos is not available for OSF.  It is only available on Ultrix at
this point.  DEC's suggestion to us (we had the same problem) was
"Buy a separate Ultrix box to run Kerberos"  (what morons).  As far as
what to do about it, we ended up using pppd on the OSF box.  There is
a port available for it put out by Steve Tate
<srt@ponder.csci.unt.edu>
machine name (zaphod.csci.unt.edu), and the file name is
/pub/newstuff/2.2.alpha/ppp-2.2a5.mine.tgz
This way, you just set up the DECServer to do a pass-through login, or
rlogin to the OSF Box, and your user's must authenticate themselves
there.  You can run PPP after they log on.  One small problem, you are
currently limited to 10 users due to a small bug in the pppd program.
It should be fixed before the final release is available (about 2
weeks).  One other alternative we are working on now is to set up a
cheap 486 clone running Linux and use it as the authentication server.
I'll let you know how that comes out.
