   nothing stands out. We've mucked with ubc_maxpercent and it made a
   marginal improvement (almost unmeasureable, actually).

Perhaps you should ensure that your datafiles of the Oracle
tablespaces and the redo logs are spread over several disks. Perhaps
it is an I/O problem (check iostat and vmstat)?

The Oracle installation guide recommends the adaptation of IPC
parameters (PW5 also uses shared memory - check ipcs).

We are running Oracle 7.1.3 and Pathworks V5f (about 5 and 50 users,
respectively) on a 3000-800 with 128 Megs, OSF/1 3.0. It's running
very smoothly!

