I just finished upgrading to 3.2 this morning. The original was 1.3, and
it came to 2.0, 3.0 and finally 3.2. I encounted some problems. That was
when from 2.0 to 3.0, the system asked me about OSF-BASE Pak. It took me
a while to dig out the original license. Also, when from 1.3 to 2.0, I
need to reset the jumper for the firmware upgrading. The average
upgrading time is around 80 minutes. Also, remember, you must have the
suitable firmware for each upgrading.

I also just finished another upgrading from 2.0 to 3.2 for two systems.
One of them was failed when upgrading form 2.0 to 3.0. The whole system
is unsalvagable and I had to reinstall the whole system. Fortunately, I
have the files backed up and I have a similar system working side by
side. Also, the OSF-BASE Pak is needed for it. Since I found the Pak for
the other system, therefor this Pak didn't bring too much trouble. But
still there was a scary moment as I have been working in OSF/1 system
for only one month.

Tingli Pan

