X-Deja-AN: 103622234
sender: news@news.demon.co.uk
x-posting-host: relay1.pipex.net
organization: Demon Internet News Service
cc: mat@intera.co.uk
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

I had this problem when taking my machine off the network for a
demo at another site.  After many attempts, I settled on the
following, which always seems to work:

In /etc/rc.config change the NIS_CONF lines from "YES" to "NO" and
from "1" to "0" as appropriate.  Reboot.

I'm sure there *must* be a published mechanism for doing
this, but I couldn't find one.

This works most of the time.  However, once I was unable to reboot
as the message 'no available ptys' was displayed.  For some reason -
I know not why - /dev/ttyp1 was missing.  The solution:

	Boot single user - boot -flags s
	mount -u /
	cd /dev
	ls -al ttyp*		(to find missing file)
	mknod ttyp1 c 6 1
	chmod 666 typ1
	logout			(may also need reboot)

